# punused findings adjudicated as false positives. One literal substring per
# line, matched against punused's output line; full-line `#` comments carry the
# reason. Invalid-by-construction classes: `.kiro/steering/tools.md`.
#
# boundedTextError is constructed at five non-test sites (certScan.visit,
# parsePrivateKeyBlock, Encode, CheckCurrency, decode) and its Unwrap runs on
# every failed conversion: the error reaches process.failEntry -> IsShutdown ->
# errors.Is(err, context.Canceled), which walks the chain through it. The
# embedded field is the `error` interface, which promotes only Error(), so
# without Unwrap every errors.As traversal past the wrapper dead-ends. The repo
# has already shipped that bug once (a wrap made IsShutdown false and logged a
# routine shutdown at ERROR). Upstream: bep/punused#3.
method (boundedTextError).Unwrap
#
# LostError.Unwrap upholds the errors.Is(err, ErrWatchLost) contract documented
# on the type and is exercised by six assertions across watch's loop, recv and
# poll suites. Honest caveat: no non-test consumer unwraps it today -- main.go's
# reportWatchExit uses errors.As on the concrete type, which matches at depth 0
# -- so removing it would change no caller's decision. Kept rather than deleted
# because the real question is whether the exported ErrWatchLost / LostError /
# Unwrap trio should collapse to just *LostError, which is an exported-surface
# design decision, not a dead-symbol cleanup.
method (*LostError).Unwrap
#
# internal/testcerts has no _test.go of its own; it is a regular package
# precisely so other packages' _test.go files can import a shared certificate
# fixture builder, which guarantees EU1001 for every symbol in it. All six are
# heavily used and none is a leftover: Mint 116 call sites, NewECDSAKey 98,
# GenerateSelfSignedCert 59, GenerateChainMaterial 48, KeyPEM 46,
# GenerateCertChain 12. GenerateCertChain and GenerateChainMaterial are not
# redundant -- the former exposes only the leaf key, the latter exists to express
# the cases identity selection must get right (issuer-owned key, renewed cert
# reusing its predecessor's key, future-dated renewal).
function Mint
function KeyPEM
function NewECDSAKey
function GenerateSelfSignedCert
function GenerateCertChain
function GenerateChainMaterial
